From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:53:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] stm32mp2: derive fdtfile from a "cargt," per-panel compatible

board_late_init() only derives fdtfile from the first compatible when
it is "st,<name>". Cargt devicetrees use "cargt,<name>", so fdtfile
came from the default environment, which names the board-wide
devicetree. After a per-panel FIP was flashed, Linux still booted the
board-wide devicetree without the panel.

Cargt per-panel devicetrees have "cargt,<dtb basename>" as first
compatible and the board-wide "cargt,<board>" as second. When both are
"cargt," and the name is an stm32mp2 DTB basename, set fdtfile to
<name>.dtb on every boot, so the running panel FIP picks the kernel
devicetree of the same name, overriding any saved fdtfile. On the
board-wide devicetree fdtfile is left alone, so a saved fdtfile
override keeps working there.

For any "cargt,<name>" first compatible, board_name is now <name>.
Before, it was the whole compatible, so on the board-wide devicetrees
board_name loses its "cargt," prefix. Nothing in the stm32mp2 U-Boot
environment reads board_name.

fdtfile is set with env_set(), as the "st," path does. It reaches the
saved environment only when something saves it, such as the bootcount
store after a RAUC install. A saved value is the panel's own DTB and is
overwritten on every boot from that FIP.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Cargt board specific]
Signed-off-by: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
---
 board/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/board/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2.c b/board/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2.c
--- a/board/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2.c
+++ b/board/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2.c
@@ -628,7 +628,36 @@ int board_late_init(void)
 		fdt_compat = fdt_getprop(gd->fdt_blob, 0, "compatible",
 					 &fdt_compat_len);
 		if (fdt_compat && fdt_compat_len) {
-			if (strncmp(fdt_compat, "st,", 3) != 0) {
+			if (strncmp(fdt_compat, "cargt,", 6) == 0) {
+				const char *name = fdt_compat + 6;
+				const char *fallback;
+
+				env_set("board_name", name);
+
+				/*
+				 * A Cargt per-panel devicetree has a first
+				 * compatible "cargt,<dtb basename>" and keeps
+				 * the board-wide "cargt,<board>" as second
+				 * compatible. Only then is this FIP tied to a
+				 * panel: force fdtfile to the matching kernel
+				 * devicetree, whatever the saved environment
+				 * says. On the board-wide devicetree, leave
+				 * fdtfile alone so a saved override still
+				 * works. The prefix check keeps a "cargt,"
+				 * name that isn't an stm32mp2 DTB basename
+				 * from producing a missing fdtfile.
+				 */
+				fallback = fdt_stringlist_get(gd->fdt_blob, 0,
+							      "compatible", 1,
+							      NULL);
+				if (strncmp(name, "stm32mp2", 8) == 0 &&
+				    fallback &&
+				    strncmp(fallback, "cargt,", 6) == 0) {
+					snprintf(dtb_name, sizeof(dtb_name),
+						 "%s.dtb", name);
+					env_set("fdtfile", dtb_name);
+				}
+			} else if (strncmp(fdt_compat, "st,", 3) != 0) {
 				env_set("board_name", fdt_compat);
 			} else {
 				env_set("board_name", fdt_compat + 3);
